mapping "L858K.1" source="L858K" target="254744006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L858K SNOMED CT 254744006 = reactive fibrous papule of fingers. No SNOMED CT concept for
        fibrous papule of finger exists; closest related entity is SNOMED CT 4110730 (254744006) Fibrous
        papule of face, which is the same lesion type but anatomically restricted to face. Target
        subsumes the lesion-type axis but not the anatomical-location axis; treated as broader (lesion
        category) at low confidence because the location mismatch is material.
        """
}
mapping "L858W.1" source="L858W" target="201416004" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L858W SNOMED CT 201416004 = other specified epidermal thickening (Swedish subcode of L85.8).
        Target SNOMED CT 40405463 (201416004) = [X]Other specified epidermal thickening. Exact semantic
        equivalence via the WHO ICD-10 X-expansion crosswalk.
        """
}
mapping "L869.1" source="L869" target="201417008" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L869 SNOMED CT 201417008 = keratoderma in diseases classified elsewhere (ICD-10 L86). Target
        SNOMED CT 40405464 (201417008) = [X]Keratoderma in diseases classified elsewhere. Exact WHO ICD-10
        X-expansion crosswalk; 1:1 equivalence.
        """
}
mapping "L889.1" source="L889" target="74578003" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L889 SNOMED CT 74578003 = pyoderma gangrenosum (ICD-10 L88). Target SNOMED CT 133283 (74578003)
        = Pyoderma gangrenosum. Verified via Athena ICD10->SNOMED CT crosswalk (45538588 -> 133283). Exact
        1:1 clinical equivalence.
        """
}
mapping "L889B.1" source="L889B" target="74578003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L889B SNOMED CT 74578003 = fagedenic/vegetans pyoderma, a clinical variant of pyoderma
        gangrenosum characterized by vegetating/frambesiform lesions. No SNOMED CT concept for or exists
        (SNOMED CT only has pemphigus/bullous variants). Best defensible target is SNOMED CT 133283 (74578003)
        Pyoderma gangrenosum, which is the parent disorder that fully subsumes this variant. Low
        confidence due to loss of the vegetans qualifier and the heterogeneity of the source entity.
        """
}
mapping "L889C.1" source="L889C" target="17732003" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L889C SNOMED CT 17732003 = ecthyma gangrenosum, a cutaneous infection typically due to
        Pseudomonas aeruginosa in immunocompromised hosts. Target SNOMED CT 4070328 (17732003) = Ecthyma
        gangrenosum. Exact 1:1 clinical equivalence; identical fully-specified name.
        """
}
mapping "L889D.1" source="L889D" target="2396006" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L889D SNOMED CT 2396006 = malignant pyoderma, a rare aggressive ulcerative dermatosis.
        Target SNOMED CT 4035767 (2396006) = Malignant pyoderma. Exact 1:1 clinical equivalence; identical
        fully-specified name.
        """
}
mapping "L889X.1" source="L889X" target="74578003" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L889X SNOMED CT 74578003 = pyoderma gangrenosum, unspecified (the unspecified specifier of
        L88). Target SNOMED CT 133283 (74578003) = Pyoderma gangrenosum. The unspecified-source maps
        cleanly to the unqualified SNOMED CT disorder; the qualifier carries no clinical distinction here
        because is itself unspecific to subtype.
        """
}
mapping "L899A.1" source="L899A" target="1186641008" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899A SNOMED CT 1186641008 = pressure ulcer of neck region. Target SNOMED CT 37162063
        (1186641008) = Pressure injury of cervical region of back. Cervical region of back corresponds
        anatomically to the neck region; close 1:1 equivalence with a small terminology convention
        difference (vs). High confidence per Athena-local match.
        """
}
mapping "L899B.1" source="L899B" target="225555001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899B SNOMED CT 225555001 = pressure ulcer of shoulder/upper arm. Target SNOMED CT 4021481
        (225555001) = Pressure injury of shoulder. The shoulder component is covered exactly; the
        upper-arm component is not separately represented in SNOMED CT. Target subsumes the shoulder axis
        of this two-region source; treated as broader with moderate confidence because the upper-arm
        coverage is implicit rather than explicit.
        """
}
mapping "L899C.1" source="L899C" target="225559007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899C SNOMED CT 225559007 = pressure ulcer of elbow/forearm. Target SNOMED CT 439410
        (225559007) = Pressure injury of elbow. Elbow component is covered exactly; the forearm
        component is not represented. Target subsumes the elbow axis only; broader with moderate
        confidence because the source spans two adjacent anatomical regions.
        """
}
mapping "L899D.1" source="L899D" target="1163215007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899D SNOMED CT 1163215007 = pressure ulcer of wrist/hand. No SNOMED CT concept exists for
        pressure injury of wrist or hand. Best available standard target is SNOMED CT 37159532 (1163215007)
        Pressure injury (the unlocated parent), which subsumes the source at the cost of losing the
        wrist/hand location specificity. Low confidence; broader climb to the unlocated parent is a
        specificity-loss fallback.
        """
}
mapping "L899E.1" source="L899E" target="225563000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899E SNOMED CT 225563000 = pressure ulcer of pelvic region (a heterogeneous region
        encompassing buttock, sacral, coccygeal, hip areas). Target SNOMED CT 200485 (225563000) = Pressure
        injury of buttock, which is the dominant anatomical subregion of the source's pelvic region.
        SNOMED CT also has 225562005 (sacral) and 699216009 (coccygeal) as narrower alternatives. Buttock
        chosen as the broadest single defensible target; broader with moderate confidence because the
        pelvic region is wider than buttock alone.
        """
}
mapping "L899F.1" source="L899F" target="699214007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source L899F SNOMED CT 699214007 = pressure ulcer of hip/thigh. No SNOMED CT concept for pressure
